Live-draw: 3D textures and zeta-aliased DEPTH16 (shadow compare), X16 and A8R8G8B8 textures.

Killzone 3's first level (pass 11 RPCS3 capture, the RE notes) uses texture paths live-draw
did not have:
- TEXTURE_FORMAT dimension 3: one A8R8G8B8 linear 3D texture in the final composite (ASSUMPTION: colour-grading
  LUT). It decoded to nothing and read SRV_WHITE. Now: decode_guest_texture_3d (uncompressed formats, base level,
  slices pitch*height apart or 3D-swizzled), a TEXTURE3D resource and SRV, cache key with dimension and depth, and
  the fragment-program decompiler's tex_cube_mask carries 3D units in bits 16..31 (Texture3D declaration, .xyz
  sampling, TXP .xyz / .w). The mask is part of the PSO key and HLSL hash through cube_mask.
- DEPTH16 (0x92/0x93) at a host-rendered Z16 zeta, zfunc GEQUAL on every bind: shadow compare. The unit binds the
  R32_FLOAT depth snapshot and rsx_fp_apply_shadow_compare rewrites its Sample call to SampleCmpLevelZero against
  texcoord.z; the root signature gains eight static comparison samplers at s16+F (F = RSX zfunc, reversed as
  RPCS3 does: GEQUAL -> LESS_EQUAL; linear, clamp).
- X16 (0x94) at a Z16 zeta: depth read as a value; binds the snapshot like DEPTH24_D8 (depth in RGB, alpha 1).
- A8R8G8B8 at a Z24S8 zeta (remap 0xAA93, point sampled): the game reads the depth bytes. Binds the snapshot and
  rsx_fp_apply_depth_argb rebuilds A=depth[23:16] R=depth[15:8] G=depth[7:0] B=stencil(0) and applies the remap
  (0xAA93 gives RGB = depth bytes high to low). zdepth_t records the zeta's depth format; Z16 zetas are excluded.
tex_zalias_kind() decides all three for both the PSO key and the bind; LD_NO_ZALIAS=1 turns them off for an A/B.
Gamma decode is not applied to shadow or depth-byte units.
Verified: tools/smoke/test_fp_d3d12.c under Proton (D3D12 device, decompiled programs + these post-passes):
tex3d 4/4 voxels, shadow-cmp 3/3, depth-argb 1/1 (remap 0xAAE4) and 1/1 (0xAA93). Not yet seen on KZ3's level (the port does not reach it).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.15.0 (SPU pass 81): context only, upstream shadow-compare branch (PR302) kept before the 3D test.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): unnorm scale: upstream 00c2999d's volume path (dim[][3], volume_mask); 2012's 3D bits (cube_mask 16..31) folded into volume_mask there too (no depth passed: skipped as before).

